{"authored" [{"question" "q-120024" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f21c4e959643b74f4a8745477363225d207b247a57dafa2d96eba6b8423755" "basis" 549 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-120024" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{16}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{16})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can simplify the given expression by rewriting the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})$ in the numerator, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})} & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})}} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f21c4e959643b74f4a8745477363225d207b247a57dafa2d96eba6b8423755" "basis" 549 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/math