"q-120058" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the exact value of $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f21c4e959643b74f4a8745477363225d207b247a57dafa2d96eba6b8423755" "basis" 549 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-120058" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f21c4e959643b74f4a8745477363225d207b247a57dafa2d96eba6b8423755" "basis" 549 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-120058" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ba5df604d4ec4d57fa20c1c7f183e0d2d8c2f4f74c8e60679ef59b5fe8918388" "basis" 549 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-120058" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f21c4e959643b74f4a8745477363225d207b247a57dafa2d96eba6b8423755" "basis" 549 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-120058" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f21c4e959643b74f4a8745477363225d207b247a57dafa2d96eba6b8423755" "basis" 549 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-120058" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f21c4e959643b74f4a8745477363225d207b247a57dafa2d96eba6b8423755" "basis" 549 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-120058" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f21c4e959643b74f4a8745477363225d207b247a57dafa2d96eba6b8423755" "basis" 549 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-120058" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f21c4e959643b74f4a8745477363225d207b247a57dafa2d96eba6b8423755" "basis" 549 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-120058" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f21c4e959643b74f4a8745477363225d207b247a57dafa2d96eba6b8423755" "basis" 549 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-120058" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f21c4e959643b74f4a8745477363225d207b247a57dafa2d96eba6b8423755" "basis" 549 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-120020" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})}{{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13952520/state.json" "file_sha256" "9b7f9219649ce8f1e238630005608d30aa9d3d81391d0b2da1b85156b0151f7a" "basis" 604 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13952520/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-120020" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{12})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can simplify the given expression by rewriting the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})$ in the numerator, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})}{{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})} & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}{{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13952520/state.json" "file_sha256" "9b7f9219649ce8f1e238630005608d30aa9d3d81391d0b2da1b85156b0151f7a" "basis" 604 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13952520/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-120020" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficu