^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({15}^{∘}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050034/state.json" "file_sha256" "5acb24329a24bfffc49a67050f08d98b093ca4125cce61eb78660ae15663ac11"} {"question" "q-24361" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={7.5}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({7.5}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {7.5}^{∘})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({7.5}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡({15}^{∘}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({15}^{∘}) & =2\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({15}^{∘}) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({15}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({15}^{∘})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with $x={15}^{∘},$ we can further simplify the above expression: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{15}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{15}^{∘}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {15}^{∘})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({30}^{∘})\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({15}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡({30}^{∘})=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050034/state.json" "file_sha256" "5acb24329a24bfffc49a67050f08d98b093ca4125cce61eb78660ae15663ac11"} {"question" "q-24361" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050034/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e9e5735bfa187a69a964b30ffbb3a2d7fc6bd674feedf05388bb3985742fbd9"} {"question" "q-24361" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050034/state.json" "file_sha256" "5acb24329a24bfffc49a67050f08d98b093ca4125cce61eb78660ae15663ac11"} {"question" "q-24361" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1+\\sqrt{3}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050034/state.json" "file_sha256" "5acb24329a24bfffc49a67050f08d98b093ca4125cce61eb78660ae15663ac11"} {"question" "q-24361" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050034/state.json" "file_sha256" "5acb24329a24bfffc49a67050f08d98b093ca4125cce61eb78660ae15663ac11"} {"question" "q-120020" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})}{{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050034/state.json" "file_sha256" "5acb24329a24bfffc49a67050f08d98b093ca4125cce61eb78660ae15663ac11"} {"question" "q-120020" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{12})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can simplify the given expression by rewriting the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})$ in the numerator, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})}{{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})} & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}{{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050034/state.json" "file_sha256" "5acb24329a24bfffc49a67050f08d98b093ca4125cce61eb78660ae15663ac11"} {"question" "q-120020" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050034/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e9e5735bfa187a69a964b30ffbb3a2d7fc6bd674feedf05388bb3985742fbd9"} {"question" "q-120020" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050034/state.json" "file_sha256" "5acb24329a24bfffc49a67050f08d98b093ca4125cce61eb78660ae15663ac11"} {"question" "